From ff2f1394c20766c345e9c89988d3b0fa7483b6c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:28:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] PCI: Disable MSI for ULi 5239 revision 01 with subsystem
 5238

On an Ultra45, the ULi 10b9:5239 EHCI controller (revision 01,
subsystem 10b9:5238) duplicates the low MSI data byte into the high
byte on word and dword writes. Word writes of 0001, 0002 and 1234
read back as 0101, 0202 and 3434; a dword write of 00000001 reads
back as 00000101. The adjacent OHCI function preserves these values.

Programming MSI 1 therefore produces a value outside the bridge's
allocated MSI range. Disable MSI so the USB PCI HCD selects INTx.
Limit the match to the tested identity; this does not establish that
the subsystem ID causes the fault or that other revisions are safe.

Signed-off-by: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
---

Observed on Ultra45, with EHCI unbound and MSI disabled:
  word 0000 -> 0000; 0001 -> 0101; 0002 -> 0202
  word 0010 -> 1010; 00a5 -> a5a5; 1234 -> 3434
  dword 00000001 -> 00000101
Independent byte reads confirmed the high byte. Writing the high byte
00 cleared it; writing 12 did not install 12. A subsequent low-byte
write of 34 read back as 0034. Byte writes are not an established general
workaround for arbitrary MSI data. Original data was restored afterward.
The adjacent OHCI function preserved word writes 0001, 0002 and 1234.

Boot testing: automatic INTx, three EHCI rebinds, hub control requests,
and 640MiB of read-only direct storage I/O with matching SHA256 pairs.
NIC MSI remained functional; taint stayed zero. Other architectures and
revisions have not been tested. The scope is intentionally conservative.

 drivers/pci/quirks.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/quirks.c b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
index de9bbccda21f..ed509775b2ef 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
@@ -1942,6 +1942,16 @@ DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_FINAL(PCI_VENDOR_ID_ATI, 0x4389, quirk_no_msi);
 DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_FINAL(PCI_VENDOR_ID_ATI, 0x438a, quirk_no_msi);
 DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_FINAL(PCI_VENDOR_ID_ATI, 0x438b, quirk_no_msi);
 
+/* This ULi EHCI revision duplicates the low MSI data byte on word writes. */
+static void quirk_uli_ehci_no_msi(struct pci_dev *dev)
+{
+	if (dev->revision == 0x01 &&
+	    dev->subsystem_vendor == PCI_VENDOR_ID_AL &&
+	    dev->subsystem_device == 0x5238)
+		quirk_no_msi(dev);
+}
+DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_FINAL(PCI_VENDOR_ID_AL, 0x5239, quirk_uli_ehci_no_msi);
+
 static void quirk_pcie_mch(struct pci_dev *pdev)
 {
 	pdev->no_msi = 1;
